   "solution_en": "<p>The number of letters (taken in alphabetical series written in Z to A i.e. reverse order) between subsequent letters starting from left to right letter in any option, are consecutive multiples of any number.</p><p>Option (a): <b>F </b><u>G H I J K L</u><b> M </b><u>N O P Q</u><b> R </b><u>S T</u><b> U</b> (for URMF, between U and R, there are 2 letters, then between R and M, there are 4, and between M and F, there are 6)</p><p>Option (b):<b> D</b> <u>E F G H I J K L M</u> <b>N</b> <u>O P Q R S T</u> <b>U</b> <u>V W X</u> <b>Y</b> (for YUND, between Y and U, there are 3 letters, then between U and N, there are 6, and between N and D, there are 9)</p><p>Option (d): <b>D</b> <u>E F G</u> <b>H</b> <u>I J</u> <b>K</b> <u>L</u> <b>M</b> (for MKHD, between M and K, there is 1 letter, then between K and H, there are 2, and between H and D, there are 3)</p><p>In option (c): this doesn't follow hence, odd. Between V and Q, it is 4 letters, between Q and H it is 8 letters, so it should be 12 letters between H and last letter, which shouldn't be A)</p>",
